    "title": "Conformal Scaling in Trained Transformer Attention: Evidence for an SYK Fixed Point",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19225996",
    "publication_date": "2026-03-25",
    "description": "We report the first empirical measurement of conformal scaling in trained transformer attention. Analyzing all 144 attention heads in GPT-2 with maximum-entropy inputs, we find that 44 heads exhibit power-law attention weight decay with R\u00b2 &gt; 0.90 and median conformal dimension \u0394 = 0.2493, matching the Sachdev-Ye-Kitaev (SYK) model prediction \u0394 = 1/4 for q = 4 interactions in one dimension. Three controls isolate contributions: reinitializing attention weights destroys all power-law structure; randomizing positional embeddings preserves the power law but shifts \u0394; structured text inputs shift the effective \u0394. GPT-2 and Pythia \u2014 architecturally distinct positional encoding schemes \u2014 both converge toward \u0394 = 1/4 with model depth. Training dynamics across three Pythia models reveal a phase transition from disordered to conformal attention. The block entanglement entropy follows S(k) = (c/3)log(k) with R\u00b2 &gt; 0.99, the entanglement structure predicted by conformal field theory. Fine checkpoint sampling reveals a prethermal plateau at \u0394 \u2248 0.50 (the SYK q=2 integrable value), suggesting a two-stage flow from disorder through integrable order toward chaos.",
